(6823084, 1026061, 43774, '<td valign="top">Yum!! I like the composition too.</td>', 'Yum!! I like the composition too.', '2012-07-20 20:09:08.000000', NULL, 1),
(6823108, 1026059, 149507, '<td valign="top">You captured nice textures in the bowl of pudding itself. This would work much better with a lot less of the background taking focus away from the main subject. The spoon in the background goes through the middle of the subject. Overall the image seems a little too pink.</td>', 'You captured nice textures in the bowl of pudding itself. This would work much better with a lot less of the background taking focus away from the main subject. The spoon in the background goes through the middle of the subject. Overall the image seems a little too pink.', '2012-07-20 20:43:09.000000', NULL, 1),
(6823112, 1026030, 149507, '<td valign="top">Your image has no focal point to draw the eye.</td>', 'Your image has no focal point to draw the eye.', '2012-07-20 20:47:08.000000', NULL, 1),
(6823115, 1026041, 149507, '<td valign="top">I really like the texture in light and dark areas on the foreground strawberries. With a dark chocolate sauce it would have been better to have a lighter plate and table to offset it. Overall the image is a bit too dark but the highlights are still a little bright -- more exposure and less contrast would help.</td>', 'I really like the texture in light and dark areas on the foreground strawberries. With a dark chocolate sauce it would have been better to have a lighter plate and table to offset it. Overall the image is a bit too dark but the highlights are still a little bright -- more exposure and less contrast would help.', '2012-07-20 20:56:20.000000', NULL, 1),
(6823125, 1025982, 149507, '<td valign="top">I like the use of color to draw the eye to the focal point. Being the focal point, it would be better if the strawberry were clear. This concept would work really well if the model and strawberry were both clear but the people in the background were out of focus and motion blurred. There are too many distracting elements in the background that could have been cropped out, particularly the sad-looking guy and the hand.</td>', 'I like the use of color to draw the eye to the focal point. Being the focal point, it would be better if the strawberry were clear. This concept would work really well if the model and strawberry were both clear but the people in the background were out of focus and motion blurred. There are too many distracting elements in the background that could have been cropped out, particularly the sad-looking guy and the hand.', '2012-07-20 21:17:59.000000', NULL, 1),
(6823140, 1025940, 149507, '<td valign="top">I rank this one near the top. I like how the different types of fruit and chocolate form layers and stripes of different colors that lead the eye diagonally across the image.</td>', 'I rank this one near the top. I like how the different types of fruit and chocolate form layers and stripes of different colors that lead the eye diagonally across the image.', '2012-07-20 21:38:55.000000', NULL, 1),
(6823150, 1025824, 149507, '<td valign="top">I love the concept and the way the photo is cropped so that the subject sits on the bottom of the frame. The backlighting is mostly even but some of the highlights are a little over-exposed.</td>', 'I love the concept and the way the photo is cropped so that the subject sits on the bottom of the frame. The backlighting is mostly even but some of the highlights are a little over-exposed.', '2012-07-20 21:50:50.000000', NULL, 1),
(6823164, 1025976, 149507, '<td valign="top">This has nice color, textures and lines.</td>', 'This has nice color, textures and lines.', '2012-07-20 21:57:34.000000', NULL, 1),
(6823165, 1025775, 149507, '<td valign="top">I really like how the color of the dessert is reflected toward the bottom of the image and balances the colors throughout the image.</td>', 'I really like how the color of the dessert is reflected toward the bottom of the image and balances the colors throughout the image.', '2012-07-20 22:00:34.000000', NULL, 1),
(6823230, 1026049, 43463, '<td valign="top">Voted earlier coming back to comment now.<br/> <br/>Mmmmm, cookies....my taste buds swing from thinking these are oatmeal cookies with frosting to ginger snaps with frosting. Either way they taste great with milk:-) Hmmm, that might have been an interesting addition to the composition - the glass of milk complementing the same vertical arrangement of the cookies. But, back the image as it stands - details are good with a warm toned backdrop to complement the cookies. To me, the tree branch shadows on the wall projects the mood of sitting out in the countryside on the bench just enjoying a bite of these cookies. My critique is that I wish that the shadows the cookies cast on the wood table were not so harsh. Don''t know what form of lighting you might have been using (flash, natural, or natural light with lamps), but there are two things I could suggest to lessen or eliminate those shadows. You could find something reflective/or a reflector to bounce the light back onto the back of the treats or take a table light/light and shine it onto the back of the treats to evenly balance the light.</td>', 'Voted earlier coming back to comment now. Mmmmm, cookies....my taste buds swing from thinking these are oatmeal cookies with frosting to ginger snaps with frosting. Either way they taste great with milk:-) Hmmm, that might have been an interesting addition to the composition - the glass of milk complementing the same vertical arrangement of the cookies. But, back the image as it stands - details are good with a warm toned backdrop to complement the cookies. To me, the tree branch shadows on the wall projects the mood of sitting out in the countryside on the bench just enjoying a bite of these cookies. My critique is that I wish that the shadows the cookies cast on the wood table were not so harsh. Don''t know what form of lighting you might have been using (flash, natural, or natural light with lamps), but there are two things I could suggest to lessen or eliminate those shadows. You could find something reflective/or a reflector to bounce the light back onto the back of the treats or take a table light/light and shine it onto the back of the treats to evenly balance the light.', '2012-07-20 22:56:40.000000', NULL, 1),
(6823256, 1025941, 43463, '<td valign="top">Voted earlier coming back to comment now. <br/> <br/>Love the angle you took this at - it adds visual interest and the splash of red ribbon that curls around it pulls the all the elements together nicely. The unwrapping of a sweet treat. Not sure how others feel about the tilt but to me the glass is tilting towards me. I can clearly see the berries and cream through the glass but that tilt is like the temptation of pushing a dessert towards one and stating "You want some, you know you do". My only critiques are that I wish that the berries and cream were stacked higher like a little mountain of sweets rising from the glass - or at least till the mint leaf on the left is resting on the rim like it does on the right. Then it would be a subtle nod that the flavor is bursting out towards you rather than having to ''peek'' over the rim to take a taste. Lastly, is those confounded reflections on glass that can really be a challenge. The only suggestions I can suggest to eliminate or minimalize them is a really good polarizer filter or shoot the composition in a light tent.</td>', 'Voted earlier coming back to comment now.  Love the angle you took this at - it adds visual interest and the splash of red ribbon that curls around it pulls the all the elements together nicely. The unwrapping of a sweet treat. Not sure how others feel about the tilt but to me the glass is tilting towards me. I can clearly see the berries and cream through the glass but that tilt is like the temptation of pushing a dessert towards one and stating "You want some, you know you do". My only critiques are that I wish that the berries and cream were stacked higher like a little mountain of sweets rising from the glass - or at least till the mint leaf on the left is resting on the rim like it does on the right. Then it would be a subtle nod that the flavor is bursting out towards you rather than having to ''peek'' over the rim to take a taste. Lastly, is those confounded reflections on glass that can really be a challenge. The only suggestions I can suggest to eliminate or minimalize them is a really good polarizer filter or shoot the composition in a light tent.', '2012-07-20 23:12:52.000000', NULL, 1),
(6823305, 1026067, 43463, '<td valign="top">Voted earlier coming back to comment now.<br/> <br/>Soft pastel hues to complement the presentation of the cheesecake perfectly. Love the off center ''triangle'' arrangement of elements and the angle all provide an interesting image for the eye to travel around and study. Lighting is great illuminating all elements. The dessert looks absolutely stunning on the plate. My only critique, and admitingly a small one but the devil is in the details, is when my eye travels back from the looking at the dessert in the background my eye does a hard stop at the cheesecake on the plate before us. It is then I notice the break in the symmetry. The cheesecake in the backdrop appears to be a triangle shape where the foreground slice is square. That is illusion of course because the tulips blocking it make it appear so. (Yeah, here is where I get so darn picky right;-) )So the nitpick suggestion is that to keep the symmetry going is to move the tulips so they don''t block the view...and it is an added bonus that we get to see/visually help ourselves to more cake:-) Still a lovely and well presented shot that is in my pick for the top four.</td>', 'Voted earlier coming back to comment now. Soft pastel hues to complement the presentation of the cheesecake perfectly. Love the off center ''triangle'' arrangement of elements and the angle all provide an interesting image for the eye to travel around and study. Lighting is great illuminating all elements. The dessert looks absolutely stunning on the plate. My only critique, and admitingly a small one but the devil is in the details, is when my eye travels back from the looking at the dessert in the background my eye does a hard stop at the cheesecake on the plate before us. It is then I notice the break in the symmetry. The cheesecake in the backdrop appears to be a triangle shape where the foreground slice is square. That is illusion of course because the tulips blocking it make it appear so. (Yeah, here is where I get so darn picky right;-) )So the nitpick suggestion is that to keep the symmetry going is to move the tulips so they don''t block the view...and it is an added bonus that we get to see/visually help ourselves to more cake:-) Still a lovely and well presented shot that is in my pick for the top four.', '2012-07-20 23:32:47.000000', NULL, 1),
(6823360, 1026027, 23394, '<td valign="top">This is a tough challenge to vote.  I''m torn between "what are <i>you</i> trying to do here" and "what do <i>I</i> expect here".  Further complicating matters is the question "what would I do here".<br/> <br/>What I would expect would be a technically strong piece of eye-candy that would present the dessert in a way that I would want to at least sample it, if not order it.  Along these lines I''m looking at technicals:  backgrounds, distracting elements, exposure, sharpness.  I''m also looking for creativity, imagination, and originality, which can make up for less than perfect technicals.<br/> <br/>So, where does this leave me with your image?<br/> <br/>Nice idea, but a little over-exposed and unbalanced.  You might want to play with some different compositions, such as moving the one on the right a little further back.  Also play with turning the one on the left some in order to get more sense of depth (with all the fruits appearing on the same plane, it''s flatter than need be).  Lastly, I would have swapped the back tart with the right tart, as the darker topping is a little off-putting.<br/> <br/>All the same, not a bad effort!</td>', 'This is a tough challenge to vote.  I''m torn between "what are you trying to do here" and "what do I expect here".  Further complicating matters is the question "what would I do here". What I would expect would be a technically strong piece of eye-candy that would present the dessert in a way that I would want to at least sample it, if not order it.  Along these lines I''m looking at technicals:  backgrounds, distracting elements, exposure, sharpness.  I''m also looking for creativity, imagination, and originality, which can make up for less than perfect technicals. So, where does this leave me with your image? Nice idea, but a little over-exposed and unbalanced.  You might want to play with some different compositions, such as moving the one on the right a little further back.  Also play with turning the one on the left some in order to get more sense of depth (with all the fruits appearing on the same plane, it''s flatter than need be).  Lastly, I would have swapped the back tart with the right tart, as the darker topping is a little off-putting. All the same, not a bad effort!', '2012-07-21 01:24:40.000000', NULL, 1),
(6823404, 1025976, 9387, '<td valign="top">I''m not crazy about this shot because I prefer things in focus. Just my personal opinion. I don''t think not having the top of this dessert in focus helps at all. Plus it is over-exposed in the white area.</td>', 'I''m not crazy about this shot because I prefer things in focus. Just my personal opinion. I don''t think not having the top of this dessert in focus helps at all. Plus it is over-exposed in the white area.', '2012-07-21 01:43:17.000000', NULL, 1),
(6823405, 1025606, 9387, '<td valign="top">Food doesn''t usually look good on black plates but the addition of the teaspoon really helped it a lot. I like your placement of the dessert on the plate. Appealing shot and the dessert looks good too!</td>', 'Food doesn''t usually look good on black plates but the addition of the teaspoon really helped it a lot. I like your placement of the dessert on the plate. Appealing shot and the dessert looks good too!', '2012-07-21 01:44:28.000000', NULL, 1),
(6823407, 1026070, 9387, '<td valign="top">I would have no idea what this was unless you stated the word in your title. To me they don''t look fresh and they don''t look like blueberries. I''m sorry but to me this is a poor execution of the challenge.</td>', 'I would have no idea what this was unless you stated the word in your title. To me they don''t look fresh and they don''t look like blueberries. I''m sorry but to me this is a poor execution of the challenge.', '2012-07-21 01:46:00.000000', NULL, 1),
(6823409, 1026049, 9387, '<td valign="top">NOthing looks clear to me in this shot and I think it should be. The white part of the cookie is also over exposed.</td>', 'NOthing looks clear to me in this shot and I think it should be. The white part of the cookie is also over exposed.', '2012-07-21 01:46:51.000000', NULL, 1),
(6823420, 1025993, 9387, '<td valign="top">I love the strawberries &amp; cream part of your photo as it is excellent especially the cream going onto the top of the strawberries. However, I''m not sure that your use of yellow was a good compliment to the rest of the photo. To me they sort of compete with one another for the spotlight in a strange way. It was taking my eye off of the real spotlight which was well done. I am not taking off points for the yellow but I wanted you to know how I felt when I viewed it.</td>', 'I love the strawberries & cream part of your photo as it is excellent especially the cream going onto the top of the strawberries. However, I''m not sure that your use of yellow was a good compliment to the rest of the photo. To me they sort of compete with one another for the spotlight in a strange way. It was taking my eye off of the real spotlight which was well done. I am not taking off points for the yellow but I wanted you to know how I felt when I viewed it.', '2012-07-21 01:50:14.000000', NULL, 1),
