(6827144, 1025993, 149433, '<td valign="top">I knew you could make it in the top ten with that picture... Congrats! Keep my fingers crossed for the next challenge! I think I already identified your picture ;-)</td>', 'I knew you could make it in the top ten with that picture... Congrats! Keep my fingers crossed for the next challenge! I think I already identified your picture ;-)', '2012-07-25 14:55:13.000000', NULL, 0),
(6827152, 1025939, 96574, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by Bear_Music:</b></div><hr/><i> NEW YORK Cheesecake in Hawaii? C''mon, man! ''Grats on blue :-) </i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>Hah<br/>Well, recipe is courtesy of Carnegie Deli so it''s as close as I can get.</td>', 'Originally posted by Bear_Music: NEW YORK Cheesecake in Hawaii? C''mon, man! ''Grats on blue :-)   HahWell, recipe is courtesy of Carnegie Deli so it''s as close as I can get.', '2012-07-25 15:12:39.000000', NULL, 0),
(6827435, 1025939, 9114, '<td valign="top">..."ate it myself too" lol....great shot!</td>', '..."ate it myself too" lol....great shot!', '2012-07-25 21:29:22.000000', NULL, 0),
(6827483, 1025939, 9114, '<td valign="top">How about sharing that recipe?<br/></td>', 'How about sharing that recipe?', '2012-07-25 21:56:51.000000', NULL, 0),
(6827505, 1025939, 96574, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by Debbi:</b></div><hr/><i> How about sharing that recipe? </i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>:)<br/> <br/>For those interested, <a href="//www.carnegiedeli.com/recipe.php" rel="nofollow" target="_blank">here''s</a> the recipe I followed.  It was pretty easy to make actually.  One step that''s not in this recipe is when the baking is done, turn off the stove and leave the cheesecake in there for 4-5 hours, making sure to not open the oven door during the entire baking and cooling down process. Then refrigerate the cake overnight. Letting it cool down slowly will prevent the cheesecake from cracking. Enjoy :)<br/><br/><i>Message edited by author 2012-07-26 04:38:35.</i></td>', 'Originally posted by Debbi: How about sharing that recipe?   :) For those interested, here''s the recipe I followed.  It was pretty easy to make actually.  One step that''s not in this recipe is when the baking is done, turn off the stove and leave the cheesecake in there for 4-5 hours, making sure to not open the oven door during the entire baking and cooling down process. Then refrigerate the cake overnight. Letting it cool down slowly will prevent the cheesecake from cracking. Enjoy :)', '2012-07-25 22:09:45.000000', '2012-07-26 05:38:35.000000', 0),
